notes: "AI-assisted development: implementation is written by Claude Code under the owner's direction. The owner decides what is admitted into the project (the approval gates) and what is published (push); an unattended judge role may merge task output outside the protected classes of ADR-0115. Commits written with AI assistance are meant to carry a Co-Authored-By trailer once the harness commit template adopts it (planned for November 2026); earlier commits, including most of those from October 2026, are under the owner's name, mostly without one."
